    "done_when": "tests/test_harness_home_carries_the_operator_config.py passes against a synthetic operator home and run directory, never reading or writing the real ~/.claude or ~/.codex and asserting both are untouched: (1) each backend's flight entry may declare the operator-home files its harness reads (a harness_home_files list whose entries name a path relative to the operator's harness home and an optional key filter), and reckon/schema/flight-defaults.yaml ships a declaration for the claude dialect (settings.json filtered to its hooks key, CLAUDE.md) and for the codex dialect (AGENTS.md, config.toml as a writable copy, rules/); (2) seeding a claude-shaped run home yields settings.json whose only top-level key is hooks, equal to the operator's, plus CLAUDE.md with the operator content; (3) seeding a codex run home yields AGENTS.md, a writable config.toml and rules/ matching the operator's; (4) a backend whose declaration names a file absent from the operator home seeds without it and without error; (5) a claude-shaped resume of a session present only under the operator projects directory leaves the transcript byte-identical under the run home at the same relative path, and codex does the same for a rollout under .codex/sessions; (6) a file already in the run home is never overwritten and a fresh launch copies no transcript. A logged live composition of a fenced clive launch plan shows settings.json with the operator's Stop hook command under its CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. The declared negative control is executed and logged. The gate adds no failures over tests/test_fenced_resume_reaches_its_harness.py, tests/test_crew_dispatch_resume.py, tests/test_every_attempt_is_supervised.py and tests/test_flight.py against the base. The evidence record carries an anchor with a table of what each dialect's declaration carries.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
    "goal": "Make a fenced run's harness home carry the operator-home files that its backend declares its harness reads, so hooks, instruction files and harness configuration survive the fence for any harness, as flight configuration rather than per-dialect code. Today seed_harness_home in reckon/_backends.py creates an empty directory, so since e4933730 fenced claude and clive workers load no ~/.claude/settings.json hooks (the worker Stop hook, native_agent_guard.py, shell_function_recursion_guard.py) and no user CLAUDE.md. A fenced codex worker would lose ~/.codex/AGENTS.md (codex reads AGENTS.md, never CLAUDE.md), config.toml and rules/. A resume cannot find a session recorded in the operator home: resuming r-20260925T062408975588-fenced-workers-smoke at 18:46 exited with 'No conversation found with session ID eb46c4e0-0ac6-4891-b9b6-6fd5fb4773e4'. What a worker loads is decided by its harness, not its model: clive runs the claude harness in front of several open-weight models, and AGENTS.md is the emerging standard for non-claude harnesses. So the file list lives in each backend's flight entry, with shipped defaults per dialect. Operator files are read at seed time and never embedded in code, settings.json is filtered to its hooks key only (no credentials, env or permissions), existing run-home files are never overwritten, and the operator home is never modified.",
